      "message": "The phone state listener has both hidden and public callbacks. This one will be a hidden callback, usable by System UI, debug menus, etc but not by public callers.\n\nHere is the callback:\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/base/telephony/java/android/telephony/PhoneStateListener.java?q\u003dPhoneStateListener\u0026sq\u003dpackage:android\u0026l\u003d580\n\nThere are numerous other hidden callbacks such as:\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/base/telephony/java/android/telephony/PhoneStateListener.java?q\u003dPhoneStateListener\u0026sq\u003dpackage:android\u0026l\u003d524\n\nBecause the LISTEN_PHY_CHAN_CONFIG is hidden, callers can\u0027t register for it, so they don\u0027t get callbacks for it, and accordingly they can\u0027t override the listener method or see this class.",
